{
 "id": "t09_live_parity",
 "family": "Audit: backtest vs live",
 "title": "Does the live code trade what was backtested?",
 "what": [
  {
   "name": "Question",
   "value_plain": "The testnet layers run their own code. Does that code fire the same signals, on the same bars and sides, as the backtest that justified each layer?",
   "label": "OURS"
  },
  {
   "name": "Days replayed",
   "value_plain": "30 DEV days, seed 20261016 (10 trend, 10 range, 10 high-volatility), 3 h warm-up each, no network.",
   "label": "OURS"
  },
  {
   "name": "Live exit rule",
   "value_plain": "Market entry, stop 1 %, target 2 %, close after 8 bars of the signal timeframe.",
   "label": "SOURCED"
  },
  {
   "name": "Exit study",
   "value_plain": "All DEV 1-minute bars, entry every 5 to 60 minutes, both sides; stop wins ties inside a bar.",
   "label": "OURS"
  }
 ],
 "how": "The live layer code is replayed bar by bar on the sampled days and each signal is matched to the backtest's own signal function (same time and side = same). Separately, the live 1 % / 2 % / 8-bar bracket is simulated on every DEV minute to see how trades end.",
 "window": "DEV only, 2022-04-01 to 2024-06-30 (sealed VALIDATION and HOLDOUT windows were not read); 30 sampled days",
 "verdict": {
  "label": "Backtests do not describe live for 5 layer families",
  "tone": "bad"
 },
 "why": [
  "volume_fvg trades the opposite side of the backtested reading: 0 of 24 matched signals have the same side (18 side differences in the table).",
  "The RSI layer trades events (cross, failure, rejection@40) that no backtest covered: 5m 384 of 461 signals, 15m 126 of 147, 1h 25 of 28.",
  "Every layer exits by one fixed 1 % / 2 % / 8-bar bracket that no backtest used. About 94 % time exits follow from that bracket alone (5m), not from bad luck.",
  "Good news: turn_of_candle, session_momentum, cvd_absorption, sr_flip and failed_msb match bit for bit (0 differences in 3,200+ signals)."
 ],
